content:
=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_3e7a — Yuki stays home all day: no long afternoon absence (fork of p_c9d4)

The parent document (p_c9d4) claimed Yuki leaves at 13:00 and returns at 17:30 on weekdays, taking keys, jacket, sunglasses, and water bottle. The evidence refutes this: on weekdays between 9:00 and 17:00, keys_yuki is found at entry_table_e1 on 6 of 7 looks, jacket_yuki at entry_hook_e1 on 6 of 7, sunglasses_yuki at entry_table_e1 on 5 of 7, and water_bottle_yuki at dish_rack_k1 on all 6 looks. Resident sightings place Yuki in the kitchen at 14:00 and 16:00 on Wednesday, and in the kitchen at 10:00 and 12:00 on Thursday. She is home.

What changed from the parent: all OUT_OF_HOUSE blocks for Yuki's personal items (keys, jacket, sunglasses, water bottle, wallet, shoes) are removed. The dog_leash OUT_OF_HOUSE block is also removed. Yuki's "afternoon errands" are either very brief (one look found her keys missing, suggesting a short trip) or she simply does not take her keys and jacket for them. The rest of the household routine (meals, TV, baking, Marco's work shift) is unchanged from the parent.

What sets this hypothesis apart: between 13:00 and 17:00 on a weekday, keys_yuki is at entry_table_e1, jacket_yuki is at entry_hook_e1, sunglasses_yuki is at entry_table_e1, and water_bottle_yuki is at dish_rack_k1. If the robot finds any of these OUT_OF_HOUSE or in a different room during that window, this document is refuted.

What would refute it: finding Yuki's keys, jacket, or sunglasses outside the house on a weekday afternoon, or finding Yuki absent from the house (no resident_2 sightings in any room) for more than 30 minutes during the 13:00–17:00 window.

